INT. SCHOOL BUS - EARLY MORNING

Empty seats, green vinyl, window glass fogged with breath. The engine idles. Rain runs down the glass.

CASSIUS WORTHINGTON (17, backpack, a skateboard on his lap) sits alone in the back row. He stares at his phone. A text from "Mom": "Don't forget your lunch."

He thumbs a reply: "Got it." Sends.

The bus driver, MS. LORRAINE PEAKE (60s, sweater, thermos), watches him in the rearview mirror.

LORRAINE
You're early.

CASSIUS
Couldn't sleep.

LORRAINE
Big day?

CASSIUS
Exam.

LORRAINE
You study?

CASSIUS
Some.

LORRAINE
That's the best anyone can do.

She pulls a lever. The door hisses open. A girl climbs aboard: WINNIE ABARA (16, braids, headphones). She nods at Lorraine, then spots Cassius and slows.

WINNIE
Is anyone sitting here?

CASSIUS
No.

She slides in across the aisle. He turns toward the window. She pulls out a notebook.

The bus lurches forward. The radio on Lorraine's dash crackles.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Bus forty-two, status?

LORRAINE
(into mic)
En route. Two on board.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Reminder: the Hendricks Street bridge is closed. Take Birch.

LORRAINE
Copy.

Winnie leans over.

WINNIE
You have the Calc exam too?

CASSIUS
Yeah.

WINNIE
I'm terrified.

CASSIUS
Me too.

She laughs, short and relieved. He grins. For a moment neither speaks, and the rain drums on the roof.

WINNIE
Do you want to quiz each other?

CASSIUS
Sure.

She flips her notebook open. He sets his skateboard on the floor.

WINNIE
Derivative of sine x?

CASSIUS
Cosine x.

WINNIE
Integral of one over x?

CASSIUS
Natural log of absolute x.

WINNIE
(impressed)
Okay, you studied more than "some."

CASSIUS
Don't tell anyone.

Lorraine, in the mirror, smiles.
